<%#
  The City pill in a screen's header. With one city there is nothing to
  pick, so it is only a label. With more, it is a link to the picker's own
  page, which is all a page without JavaScript needs. With JavaScript the
  same picker is already here, in a <dialog>, and the tap opens it as a
  sheet over the screen: drawn with the page rather than fetched on the tap,
  so it opens at once and a slow network costs nothing but the page itself.
  Its counts are one Grid per city for today, which the dates build anyway
  for their own.

  `back` is where a pick lands. `count`, when a screen passes it, is how
  many clubs that screen lists, and the pill says "Tbilisi · 10" instead of
  wearing the pin — the directory's form of it.

  It lives in a header, which sits outside every form on these screens —
  the new watch's included — so the picker can be a form of its own.
%>
<% count ||= nil %>
<% label = count ? "#{current_city} · #{count}" : current_city %>
<% if city_switch? %>
  <a class="city-pill<%= " city-pill--count" if count %>" href="/city?back=<%= ERB::Util.url_encode(back) %>" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="City: <%= h(current_city) %><%= ", #{count_label(count, "club")}" if count %>. Change city" data-city-sheet>
    <% unless count %><span class="city-pill__pin"><%= icon(:pin, size: 15) %></span><% end %>
    <span><%= h(label) %></span>
    <span class="city-pill__chev"><%= icon(:chevron, size: 14) %></span>
  </a>
  <dialog class="city-sheet" id="city-sheet" aria-labelledby="city-title">
    <%= erb :_city_picker, locals: { back:, mode: :sheet } %>
  </dialog>
<% else %>
  <span class="city-pill<%= " city-pill--count" if count %>">
    <% unless count %><span class="city-pill__pin"><%= icon(:pin, size: 15) %></span><% end %>
    <span><%= h(label) %></span>
  </span>
<% end %>
